  "content": {
    "title": "Where to watch Sebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman tonight? PPV info",
    "text": "March 28, 2026, 5:01 a.m. CTSebastian Fundora will defend his WBC junior middleweight title against Keith Thurman in Las Vegas on March 28.The main card will air live on Prime Video pay-per-view for $74.99.Ring walks for the main event are expected around 10 p.m. CT.Keith Thurman has his eyes on one last title reign as he returns to the ring for just the third time in the past six years to challenge defending WBC junior middleweight champion Sebastian \"The Towering Inferno\" Fundora.The pair were originally slated to box last October, before Fundora suffered a hand contusion just two weeks out from fight night which delayed the bout five months. Prior to the injury, Fundora had stopped Tim Tszyu in the seventh round of their rematch last July, successfully defending his WBC belt for a second time.Thurman, a former unified welterweight champion, had gone three years without a bout when he returned to the ring last March and scored a third-round technical knockout against Brock Jarvis in Australia. Despite his relative inactivity in recent years, Thurman believes his experience will shine through against Fundora.“I’ve been favorited in the majority of all of my fights, but at the end of the day, being the hunter is a lot of fun,\" Thurman said at the final press conference. \"I’m on the prowl. There’s nothing like becoming world champion by taking it from the previous world champion, especially a highly qualified world champion like Fundora.\"Here's how to watch the Fundora vs. Thurman fight card.Watch Sebastian Fundora vs. Keith Thurman on Prime Video PPVWhere to watch Sebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman tonight?The Sebastian Fundora vs. Keith Thurman headlined fight card will air live on Prime Video pay-per-view, while three preliminary fights will stream free on Prime Video ahead of the main card. The pay-per-view is also available through traditional cable and satellite outlets.How to watch: Prime Video PPVSebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman pay-per-view pricePBC's four-fight card from Las Vegas is available on Prime Video pay-per-view, as well as through traditional cable and satellite outlets, for $74.99.PPV price: $74.99What time is Sebastian Fundora vs Keith Thurman fight tonight?The PBC on Prime Video pay-per-view card is set to begin at 7 p.m. (CT) on March 28, with ring walks for the main event expected at approximately 10 p.m. (CT). Three preliminary fights will air free on Prime Video beginning at 4:30 p.m. (CT).PPV start: 7 p.m. CTFundora vs. Thurman ring walks: approx. 10 p.m. CTFundora vs Thurman undercardSebastian Fundora (23-1-1, 15 KOs) vs. Keith Thurman (31-1, 23 KOs); WBC junior middleweight titleYoenis Tellez (11-1, 8 KOs) vs. Brian Mendoza (23-4, 17 KOs)Yoenli Hernandez (9-0, 8 KOs) vs. Terrell Gausha (24-5-1, 12 KOs)Gurgen Hovhannisyan (9-0, 8 KOs) vs. Cesar Navarro (15-3, 13 KOs)Preliminary fights (free on Prime Video)Elijah Garcia (17-1, 13 KOs) vs. Kevin Newman II (18-3-1, 11 KOs)Kaipo Gallegos (11-0-1, 9 KOs) vs. Julian Gonzalez (16-1-1, 12 KOs)Brayan Gonzalez (4-0, 3 KOs) vs. Brandon Guerrero (7-4)Fundora vs Thurman oddsFundora enters his third title defense as a -380 favorite, while Thurman is a +280 underdog to win the title. The over/under is set at 9.5 rounds.Fundora by KO/TKO: -125Fundora by decision: +255Thurman by KO/TKO: +650Thurman by decision: +600Odds via DraftKings, as of March 27Boxing this weekendMoses Itauma vs. Jermaine Franklin; 1 p.m. (CT), March 28; DAZNSebastian Fundora vs. Keith Thurman; 7 p.m. (CT), March 28, Prime Video PPVHarrison Campbell covers boxing for The Tennessean and high school sports for The Daily Herald. Email him at hcampbell@usatodayco.com and follow him on Twitter @hccamp.",
